<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ariovistus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ariovistus was a Germanic leader of the Suebi who crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> around 70 BCE as an ally of the Sequani and Arverni against the Aedui. After defeating the Aedui he settled his people on Sequanian land, and in 59 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> recognised him as king and friend. In 58 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> defeated him in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a> and drove his army back across the Rhine.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ariovistus.jpg" alt="Ariovistus" width="216" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Peter Johann Nepomuk Geiger · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caesar_and_Ariovistus_(meeting_before_the_battle)_by_Johann_Nepomuk_Geiger_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
